+;; missing-tag-properties checks only the tag-property pairs the owner expects to be filled: the
+;; tag-properties input, else the Worker's HEALTH_TAG_PROPERTIES variable, which render-wrangler.mjs
+;; writes from the HEALTH_TAG_PROPERTIES GitHub variable or config/settings.json
+;; health.expectedTagProperties. Each pair is resolved before any check runs. A bad input pair
+;; refuses the call naming its entry. The stored pairs serve every graph on the Worker, so a stored
+;; pair that doesn't resolve in this graph is skipped and named under skipped instead; a malformed
+;; variable still refuses.
